<title>CANADA: Molson locks out workers at Ontario plant.</title>
<headline>Molson locks out workers at Ontario plant.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Molson Cos Ltd said Sunday it had locked out 500 union workers at its Etobicoke, Ontario brewery after contract talks collapsed.</p>
<p>The beer brewer said it &quot;remains commited, however, to reaching a settlement and continues to encourage dialogue with the union.&quot;</p>
<p>Contract talks failed to reach a deal after two months and a strike or lock-out has been legally authorized since January 27. The previous labor contract expired December 31.</p>
<p>Molson said it implemented an alternative supply plan so customers would not be affected.</p>
</text>
